Subject: Audio: play the game's mix, resample voices, fold 5.1 down

No game audio was heard: the XAudio2 path submitted only the runtime's own mixer. The EP output
is now collected and submitted in whole buffers (eight instead of three). Voices are resampled
at their rate (the 22.05 kHz ADPCM voices played 2.18 times too fast), and DirectSound's 5.1
speaker bins use the standard downmix instead of summing every bin, which clipped. The DSP
doorbell is registered when DirectSound downloads its effects image (prehook on 00580363).
RECOMP_APU_LEVELS=1 logs levels, underruns and dropped buffers about every 10 s.

Its changes to src/apu/apu_core.c, apu_dsp.c and apu_vp.c, from xemu, are licensed
LGPL-2.1-or-later (patches/README.md).

---
